WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.620
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.290
the Kingdom of Chin launched
an invasion of the land of Gi.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.330
Their opponent: the legendary general Ren Pa.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.160
The young commanders
stepped onto a relentless battlefield,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.830
their sights set on a major victory.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.540
In the first battle on the Rui Plains,
Mou Gou's central army

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.410
found itself at the mercy of a devilish scheme

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.330
contrived by the crafty Gen Pou,
one of Ren Pa's Big Four.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:18.950
Only the Hi Shin and Gyoku Hou Forces
retaliated, but made no headway;

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.910
the central army suffered a staggering defeat.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:33.200
They toyed with us... and left us in pieces!

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.750
Dammit... damn it all!

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:42.040
If this continued, a drop in morale
would be all but guaranteed.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.750
However...

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.620
The Hi Shin and Gyoku Hou Forces

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.910
refused to back down in the face
of the enemy's devious plot,

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:02.790
instead destroying them with
their fiercely courageous attack!

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:08.540
The enemy fled, and our army's
casualties were kept to a minimum.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.950
I'd call this a victory!

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:20.620
Mou Gou's army held up Shin and
Ou Hon to stave off flagging morale.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.250
They emphasized how the two units
drove off the main enemy forces,

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.790
and boasted of their feat.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.660
Those troops who knew of the defeat
needed to be inspired,

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:34.290
to be moved to add their voices
to the resounding cheers.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.450
More like public humiliation.
Behold the two fools who drove off the foe!

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:46.000
And you got yourself hurt--
must be doubly embarrassin' for you, huh?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.660
Your appearance is what's embarrassing.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.750
You'll drop everyone's morale
with that dirt-poor look of yours.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.200
You son of a bitch!

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.410
Back off. I don't trust myself right now.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.500
--Cut that out, you two!
--Hands off my injury!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.040
Mou Ten, sir...

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.290
It all worked out.
If they hadn't attacked the main force,

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:08.790
we would have wound up
with a lot more casualties.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.870
They've set themselves apart a bit,
that's for sure...

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.330
not that we even got our turn this time.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:23.250
It's a tad forced, but as long
as it keeps morale up, I'm happy.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:28.160
Besides, it's time for my twin swords

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.620
to make their move.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.580
Keep your head...

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.870
no need to hurry, Mou Gou.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:47.390
"Marauder vs. Strategist"

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:52.870
On day two, Mou Gou's central army,
having suffered a major defeat

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.330
in their first sortie,

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.660
was hurriedly putting its squads back together.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.540
Get moving, Hi Shin Unit! You're over there!

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.330
We're goin', we're goin'! Sheesh!

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.830
A-Attention!

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.750
Don't rush, now! You'll trip and hurt yourself!

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.290
General Mou Gou!

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.450
It's Haku Rou!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:26.620
Haku Rou himself has come to rally us onward!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.000
I'm here to share one of our tactics with you.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.540
Tactics?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.910
And that's defense!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.040
Defense?

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.370
The lieutenants deployed to the
left and right of the battlefield

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.290
will soon be entering the fight.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.660
Both of their armies
will be tearing into the enemy,

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:00.040
fighting their way to the main camp.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.330
Thus we in the central army
must dedicate ourselves to defense

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:08.040
until the right opportunity presents itself.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.370
Keep me safe and we win!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.660
For this reason,

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:17.620
you must fight with all your might,
so your units stay together.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:21.950
By so doing, you will safeguard
your own lives as well.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.120
Is that understood, my troops,

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.330
my comrades,

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.250
my brothers,

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.410
my sons?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.950
It was a typically Mou Gou-style appeal.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:48.910
This un-general-like way of
speech shook the very hearts

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:50.950
of the rank-and-file troops.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.580
It was on this day

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.870
that the fighting began
on the sides of the battlefield.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.660
The first to make his move was...

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.040
Report!

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.750
General Kyou En's right-flank
army has entered into battle

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.120
with the enemy's left-flank army
led by Ou Sen!

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.660
So it's begun!

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.000
It was all General Kyou En's doing!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.540
"Kyou En, Gi General,
Right Flank (40,000 Troops)"

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:30.800
"Ou Sen, Chin General,
Left Flank (40,000 Troops)"

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.910
So they're evenly matched in troop strength.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:44.200
But don't take us lightly, Ou Sen!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:49.700
Kyou En, one of my Big Four,
has a formidable trick up his sleeve...

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.450
Go into the valley! We'll surround
their right flank from below!

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:07.580
Kyou En moves his troops with arrows...

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.950
And an arrow in Kyou En's ten fingers

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:14.700
flies twice as far as anyone else's
in the Middle Kingdom.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.450
Which means Kyou En

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:19.410
can control several units at once

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:22.620
as they run between mountains.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:22.620
E-Enemy attack from the left!

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:24.160
They're coming from below, too!

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.450
We're surrounded!

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:32.120
Any general would be taken aback
by the force of Kyou En's attack.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:38.040
His army even had <i>me</i> scratching
my head back in the day!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:43.540
Normally these troops would be kept
in check and fall prey to Kyou En,

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:49.250
but I doubt that'll happen this time...
eh, Ou Sen?

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:58.120
Let's see your true power--
that which Ou Ki swore

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.910
put you on a par with
Chin's six great generals...

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:03.830
Report!

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.250
Ou Sen's army is being repelled!

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:09.580
The front line is breaking down
in the face of the enemy's attacks!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.830
What?! General Mou Gou, sir!

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:20.790
Nobody fret, now.
Ou Sen is made of far more than this.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:30.910
Report!

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:34.910
General Kai Shi Bou's front lines
are seeing movement!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.540
So they're starting, too, eh?

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.200
One target left, then: Kan Ki.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.730
"Kan Ki, Chin General, Right Flank"

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.490
"Kai Shi Bou, Gi General, Left Flank"

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.250
Report!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:05.200
The first unit has been attacked--
and there are many other casualties!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.910
What?! And the reinforcements?

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.500
W-Well, they withdrew as soon
as the first unit was attacked

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.910
and have gone into hiding.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:15.910
They <i>what</i> ?!

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.290
This was how Kan Ki fought.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.750
Rather than strike from the front,

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.370
his squadron split into smaller
subunits and went into hiding

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:33.330
before unleashing sneak attacks.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:36.200
Using the element of surprise,
they struck suddenly, then retreated--

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.040
over and over, day or night.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.370
If Gi troops happened to get in too deep,

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.540
Kan Ki's men rose up as one to destroy them,

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.080
as though they'd been waiting for the chance.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.000
Kai Shi Bou had heard the man was dauntless,

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.660
but these irregular attacks puzzled him.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:59.410
Afterward, both the central army
and Ou Sen's troops

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:02.540
fought their way to deadlocks,

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:07.410
but reports came daily of victories
won by Kan Ki's army.

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.870
Then, on the fourth day...

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.580
Report!

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.160
General Kan Ki's unit has attacked
another enemy supply division!

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:19.200
That's a very Kan Ki thing to do!

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.580
I can almost see the faces of those
poor inconvenienced enemy generals!

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.540
This tactic really makes
the most of his robber past, eh?

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:36.330
A thousand pardons.
It was a slip of the tongue.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.620
Very well.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:42.000
Surely Ren Pa isn't just standing
on the sidelines watching all this.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.410
It's about time for him to make a new move,

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:50.540
and this battle is do or die for both of us.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.080
I'm counting on you, Kan Ki...

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:58.160
Another nice haul, boss!

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:02.910
Damn you...

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:05.580
Cowardice is all you've ever known...

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.790
...you filthy Chin monkeys.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.660
Shut up, you worm.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.910
Let's see...

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.160
Our little present should be
arriving right about now.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:32.160
The surprise attacks weren't
the only thing worrying Kai Shi Bou.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.160
There was more.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:37.580
W-We've received another one...

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.540
Who's this?

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.080
The thousand-man commander
from the eighth unit.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:44.910
He went missing two days ago.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.830
And in the bags?

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.870
Well, uh, you see...

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.700
Open them.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.700
Sir!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.410
I wouldn't do that if I were--

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:56.540
Out of the way!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.330
You mean <i>all</i> of those bags...

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.660
Report! Another one has arrived!

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:16.660
I-It contains...

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:17.660
Enough!

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:24.540
Normally such atrocities
would raise the enemy's morale,

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:27.250
but this--this is going too far.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:29.830
Frankly, if we've come to this point,

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.290
the troops will instead

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.290
be terrified of Kan Ki.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.120
A tricky opponent, to be sure:

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.500
Kan Ki the Headhunter...

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.000
"Kan Ki"

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:05.370
What are <i>you</i> fretting about, eh?

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:09.200
You, Ren Pa's right-hand man?

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.330
Hardly worthy of heading up the Big Four!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.580
Gen Pou!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.160
General Gen Pou?

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.750
It's General Gen Pou!

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.660
Gen Pou, sir, what brings you here?

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:28.620
This left flank of yours.
I'll be taking it over for a while.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.330
On our lord's orders?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:36.540
Mm-hmm.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:42.160
Don't let it get to you.
Your might is beyond reproach.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:47.290
But if the left flank lags behind,
it'll affect the whole battle.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:51.250
It's all about finishing this up
and moving on to the next.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:52.450
See...

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.080
your more traditional attack style
isn't a good fit

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:59.200
for Kan Ki's peculiar approach.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:06.040
I see--so that's why you're here.
A schemer for a schemer, right?

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:11.160
Hmph. Don't lump me in with him.
Those mind games? A cheap trick.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:17.160
I'll show him the importance
of <i>real</i> military strategy!

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.620
That should do it. Let's go.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:31.000
Tell them about this place.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.000
Got it.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.330
Boss!

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.000
Their main camp is on the move!

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.910
And they're headed straight for

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.370
<i>our</i> main camp!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:49.870
Strange... Their camp should be
hidden in some hard-to-find spot,

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:52.080
as usual.

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.750
We've heard from a third party
that their left flank

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:57.950
is now being led by Gen Pou.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:03.370
The guy who did in the central army
on the first day, huh?

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:08.450
Gen Pou is Ren Pa's top strategist. Boss...

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:24.200
His strategy has a fatal flaw.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.080
The Kan Ki army is a cloud of flies,
swarming the Gi army

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:31.250
with little fragments of their military muscle.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:35.450
They send us dead bodies to crush our morale;

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:40.040
once it hits bottom, they regroup
and attack as one big squadron.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.750
But that's too slow, you imbeciles...

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:49.950
A scattered army means we can
waltz in and eliminate their main camp.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:53.250
Just that--and this battle is over.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.660
Using their own tactics against them...

00:16:55.660 --> 00:17:00.160
B-But Kan Ki's main forces
moved into the mountains

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.620
when the battle began.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:05.450
We've been searching for them all this time.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:10.160
Naturally. They're using
this strategy only because

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:12.870
they're counting on never being found.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:16.160
It's not the kind of thing you
find by looking for it.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:22.160
But look at the terrain, where we are,
and where they've struck,

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.040
and...

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.870
Here. This is where Kan Ki's main camp is.

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:31.660
Kai Shi Bou, take over the main army
and go after his head.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:32.660
Yes, sir!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:42.040
Leave it to Gen Pou...

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.040
We've found you, Kan Ki!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:51.040
Holding firm, eh?

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.700
He knew we were closing in, yet he didn't run--

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.250
he's got guts, I'll give him that...

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.040
that, and so much more!

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.830
Troops, onward!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:15.000
A message!

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:18.580
A report for Gen Pou!

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:22.750
Kai Shi Bou's main army has attacked
the main enemy camp!

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:27.500
Oho! Already? It's just
as you surmised, Gen Pou!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.660
Then it's over.

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:36.040
Once they cross swords,
it's no use for Kan Ki to cook up

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:39.750
any of his shrewd little schemes--
no matter how brave he is.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.450
They can't get to Kai Shi Bou!

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.790
No...

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:02.950
In any case, his foe-smashing power
is equal to that of Ren Pa...

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.290
What's this?

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:13.450
Why do you messengers have

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.040
blood on your armor?!

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:21.620
Good eye, old-timer.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.500
Kan Ki?

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.660
That's right.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.950
Any last words, old-timer?

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:52.950
Disguising yourself as an enemy soldier
to infiltrate their ranks

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:57.620
is no substitute for proper strategy, you fool.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.120
Not to mention a commander doing it himself.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:04.660
Strategy? Who needs strategy?

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:08.580
I just do whatever my opponent hates.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:13.620
Plus, I've always been good at this--

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:16.040
sneaking in when nobody's home.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:23.500
You may be ignorant,
but you aren't without aptitude...

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.830
I could let you be my apprentice, Kan Ki.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.500
Yeah, right,

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.750
you nobody.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:44.250
Don't stand down!

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.620
Protect your position
with everything you've got!

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.080
Shin!

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.290
Do you hear that?

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:57.660
A gong?

00:20:57.660 --> 00:21:00.040
Yes--probably the enemy's.

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:07.330
Sir, something's happened to the enemy.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.790
That gong

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:15.450
was delivering a message
from the main Gi forces

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:18.370
to every battlefield.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:25.160
Thus all of Ren Pa's generals
got the news at about the same time:

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:29.290
Gen Pou, one of the Big Four, had been killed.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.750
It can't be...

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.660
Gen Pou--killed?

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:41.950
Wasn't Gen Pou at the main camp?

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.200
How can this be?

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:50.500
No... Th-That's impossible...

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:59.080
Kan Ki made himself scarce
right after killing Gen Pou!

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.080
What?!

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:04.370
Then it's conceivable Kan Ki
could be going after <i>this</i> camp, too?

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:14.080
You've done it now, Kan Ki...
and the Chin army...

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:19.870
Let's... let's recall our generals
for now and regroup...

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:21.250
No need!

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:27.160
Night is falling. Let the squadrons
camp out where they are.

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:28.750
But Ren Pa, sir--

00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:33.370
Losing Gen Pou means I need
to rethink our fighting style.

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:35.700
Alert me if anything comes up.

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:39.120
Forgive me, Gen Pou...

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.290
I let you die such a mundane death.

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:45.080
Though I can't say these soft-hearted
things on the battlefield,

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:49.040
to lose someone with whom
I'd cheated death all those times...

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:54.040
But I won't be pining for you, Gen Pou.

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:59.620
I'm about to pay Chin back--
with their soldiers' corpses!

00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:10.620
Now I've paid you back--

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:15.330
No, now I'm one move ahead of you, Ren Pa.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"Mou Ten's Proposal"
